14.3 The effects in every set
What do the steps rest on? Four tables of Δd, computed here once for all outcomes and sets, since the table at the end counts across them; each outcome section below takes its rows from them. First the Δd of the three composites in the four windows, in every set (Step 1):

robust_delta_d &lt;- sample_sets |&gt;
  select(set, data) |&gt;
  cross_join(windows) |&gt;
  mutate(table = pmap(list(data, pre, post), \(d, a, b)
    delta_d(d, a, b, composites))) |&gt;
  select(set, pre, post, table) |&gt;
  unnest(table) |&gt;
  mutate(window = str_c(pre, " to ", post))

The same with the standard deviation of all questionnaires before the window (Step 2):

robust_delta_d_all &lt;- sample_sets |&gt;
  select(set, data) |&gt;
  cross_join(windows) |&gt;
  mutate(table = pmap(list(data, pre, post), \(d, a, b)
    delta_d(d, a, b, composites, sd_pre = "all"))) |&gt;
  select(set, pre, post, table) |&gt;
  unnest(table) |&gt;
  mutate(window = str_c(pre, " to ", post))

The Δd of the 23 scales in the two training windows, in every set, with the standard deviation of the pairs (Step 1) and of all questionnaires (Step 2):

robust_scales &lt;- sample_sets |&gt;
  select(set, data) |&gt;
  cross_join(training_windows) |&gt;
  mutate(table = pmap(list(data, pre, post), \(d, a, b)
    delta_d(d, a, b, scales$scale))) |&gt;
  select(set, pre, post, table) |&gt;
  unnest(table) |&gt;
  mutate(window = str_c(pre, " to ", post))

robust_scales_all &lt;- sample_sets |&gt;
  select(set, data) |&gt;
  cross_join(training_windows) |&gt;
  mutate(table = pmap(list(data, pre, post), \(d, a, b)
    delta_d(d, a, b, scales$scale, sd_pre = "all"))) |&gt;
  select(set, pre, post, table) |&gt;
  unnest(table) |&gt;
  mutate(window = str_c(pre, " to ", post))

How many pairs does each set keep? The persons who answered at both waves of a window, experimental + control, for Listening and Togetherness:

robust_delta_d |&gt;
  filter(outcome == "H1_ListeningTogetherness") |&gt;
  mutate(pairs = str_c(n_EG, " + ", n_CG)) |&gt;
  select(window, set, pairs) |&gt;
  pivot_wider(names_from = set, values_from = pairs)

















